<Layout title="An internet with room for everyone"><section class="shell page-section"><article class="max-w-2xl"><span class="eyebrow">Small by design. Open by nature.</span><h1 class="display page-title mt-4 mb-7">Good work needs<br/>a little breathing room.</h1><div class="prose-copy">Feedme is an open-source home for the things people make and the lives behind them. A project, a practice, a rent payment, a wild idea. You choose where a little support would make a difference.

There are no all-or-nothing campaigns. Support is a tip and a vote of encouragement, never a promise of delivery or ownership. Creators keep tips regardless of whether they reach an aspiration.

You can tip anonymously without an account. To give with your name, follow creators, or share a public message, use your Bluesky account. Feedme connects to the same open social network through AT Protocol, while each creator runs their own tipping site. Payments happen on Stripe’s hosted checkout; private receipts and notes use Habitat.

Choose a one-time tip, or keep supporting every month or year. Your chosen project split repeats with each payment, and you can stop renewals anytime. This release focuses on individual creators. Discover people across independent Feedme sites using your Bluesky connections.</div><div class="panel mt-8"><h2 class="section-title mb-3">A small home you can own.</h2><p class="muted text-sm">Built with TypeScript, Astro, Tailwind, and ordinary HTML. Self-host with Node or Docker on a VPS or Railway. No React runtime, no required browser JavaScript, no platform fee added by Feedme. Stripe and hosting fees still apply.</p></div><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mt-7"><a class="button" href="/">Explore what’s growing</a><a class="button secondary" href="/bluesky">Why Bluesky?</a></div></article></section></Layout>
